laurel 2159: measured GPU busy time and core clock in the RedwoodGPU 5 s line.
Boot 07:45 [V]: "the GPU worked 0 us on each of 0 (0 under 0.1 ms, ...)" in every line: redwood_gpu_worked() was a stub, so
nothing said whether a frame waits for the GPU or for the CPU, and the core clock (300 MHz from GPLL0 / 2) was never measured
(negroni lesson: the A730 ran at about 5 MHz for days). Each submission is now framed by two CP time stamps of the always-on
counter (19.2 MHz) in the fence page (CP_REG_TO_MEM CP_ALWAYS_ON_COUNTER before the IBs, CP_EVENT_WRITE RB_DONE_TS after
them, as Mesa/Turnip time queries on a6xx); done submissions are added up under hw_lock (busy = union of [start, end]) and fill
the existing "the GPU worked N us on each of M (histogram)" fields. CP perf counter 0 (ALWAYS_COUNT, already selected by
hw_init_regs) gives the core clock: cycles over the busy time and over the wall time of the window. New end of the line:
"; GPU busy B %, core C MHz while busy, W MHz over the window". A stamp that is not written (or > 1 s) is not counted and the
line says "(some submissions not timed)"; the GPU work itself is unchanged. 10 more ring dwords per submission.

